# Bash commands Crush may run without a permission prompt.
# Read by allow-commands.sh (PreToolUse hook). One entry per line: a
# whitespace-separated word prefix, matched word-for-word against the start
# of the command. `gh pr view` allows `gh pr view 42 --json title`, not
# `gh pr viewer` and not `gh -R o/r pr view`.
#
# Only read-only commands belong here. Any command containing a shell
# metacharacter (; & | < > ` $ ( ) { } \ or a newline) is never
# auto-allowed, whatever it starts with, so an entry cannot be chained
# into something else.
#
# MCP tools are not listed here: they go in permissions.allowed_tools in
# home-manager/modules/tools/crush.nix, crush's native per-tool allowlist.

gh pr view
